<h1>Hilchos Tzitzis</h1>
<h2>Halacha 2</h2>

<p class="no-indent" style="text-align:center; font-style:italic; margin-bottom:28px;">
The matter of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, according to what our Rebbe, his light shine, said in Likutay Tinyana, Siman 12, on the verse: "<span class="key-term">V'ayeih haseh l'olah</span>" — "And where is the lamb for the offering?" <span class="source">(Bereishis 22:7)</span> — see there well.
</p>

<!-- =============== Section 1 =============== -->
<h3>§ 1</h3>

<p>And the general principle is that even filthy places and houses of idol worship also receive vitality from the Creator, blessed be His Name. And even though His glory, blessed be His Name, is distant from there, in the aspect of: "<span class="transliteration">Uch'vodi l'acher lo etein</span>" — "And My glory I will not give to another" <span class="source">(Yeshayahu 42:8)</span> — nevertheless, they receive vitality from the aspect of the <span class="bold-concept"><span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span></span> <span class="bracket-def">[the sealed / hidden utterance]</span>, which is "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>" <span class="bracket-def">[In the beginning — counted as a creative utterance even though it does not explicitly say "G-d said"]</span>. This is the aspect of the supernal <span class="key-term">Kavod</span> <span class="bracket-def">[glory]</span>, which is sealed and concealed with the ultimate concealment. And from there they receive vitality.</p>

<p>And when a person falls there, G-d forbid, then when he begins to seek and search — "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span> [Where] is the place of His glory?" — this is his <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> and his rectification. For he returns and ascends to the supernal <span class="key-term">Kavod</span> mentioned above, which is "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span> — the place of His glory" — from which those places receive vitality, on account of the tremendous concealment. And now he returns and attaches himself to this holiness, and receives vitality from there, and ascends through this. See there well.</p>

<p>And this is considered a <span class="key-term">korban olah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[burnt offering]</span>, which atones for sinful musings of the heart — which is the aspect of "<span class="transliteration">libi s'charchar</span>" — "my heart races" — through the <span class="key-term">klipas Nogah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the shell of luminescence — the realm between holiness and impurity]</span>, etc. And through the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span> — the place of His glory" mentioned above, which one seeks and searches in those very places — through this one is rectified and atoned, as above, and from this is fashioned the aspect of a <span class="key-term">korban olah</span>, in the aspect of: "<span class="transliteration">V'ayeih haseh l'olah</span>" — "And where [<span class="key-term">ayeih</span>] is the lamb for the offering?" And this is the aspect of: "<span class="zohar-quote">Bereishis bara tayish</span>" — "In the beginning He created a goat" <span class="source">(end of Tikkunim, 2)</span> — namely, the lamb for the offering that is fashioned from the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>," which is the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," etc., as above. See there all of this well.</p>

<!-- =============== Section 2 =============== -->
<h3>§ 2</h3>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, which are the rectification of the garments — a protection from the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>, as is brought.<sup>1</sup> That is: the garments are the aspect of <span class="key-term">Kavod</span>, for Rabbi Yochanan called his garments "<span class="key-term">mechabdusai</span>" <span class="bracket-def">[my honorers]</span> <span class="source">(Shabbos 113a)</span>, and as our Rebbe, his light shine, said elsewhere.<sup>2</sup> And all the aspects of <span class="key-term">Kavod</span> of all the Ten Utterances — they all receive from the aspect of the supernal Utterance, which is "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>," the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, from which vitality is drawn even to the external places, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, the garments — which are in the aspect of <span class="key-term">Kavod</span> — are rectified through the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, which are the aspect of the supernal <span class="key-term">Kavod</span>, the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>" — the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>. This is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> of lamb's wool, which emerge from the aspect of: "And where [<span class="key-term">ayeih</span>] is the lamb for the offering?" — for the wool of sheep and lambs emerges from a very exalted level, as brought in the Writings [of the Arizal],<sup>3</sup> in the aspect of: "<span class="transliteration">Us'ar reishei k'amar naki</span>" — "And the hair of His head was like clean wool" <span class="source">(Daniel 7:9)</span>. And this level is the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," as is known.<sup>4</sup> And from there comes the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> that are made from wool, which are the aspect of hairs — the aspect of "the hair of His head," etc., as above. That is, they are in the aspect of the supernal Utterance mentioned above. And because it is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span> [sealed utterance], therefore their illumination is only in the aspect of hairs, which are sealed, and their illumination is through a very great contraction — the aspect of a <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>.</p>

<p>And these <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> rectify the garments of glory, for all aspects of <span class="key-term">Kavod</span> receive from there, as above. And they are a protection from the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>, and they rectify the sinful musings of the heart, as it is written: "And you shall see it… and you shall not stray after your hearts," etc. <span class="source">(Bamidbar 15:39)</span>. For the primary rectification of sinful musings of the heart is through the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>" — from which they [the impure places] receive their vitality, and through this very thing they are rectified. And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, which are in the aspect of: "And where [<span class="key-term">ayeih</span>] is the lamb for the offering?" — as above.</p>

<p>And this is what is written: "And you shall see it, and you shall remember all the <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span> of Hashem" <span class="source">(Bamidbar 15:39)</span>. For all the <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span> depend on this, since the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are in the aspect of the supernal Utterance — "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>" — which encompasses all the [Ten] Utterances, which are the totality of the entire Torah.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> being around the person on his four sides — to rectify the aspect of: "<span class="transliteration">V'nogah lo saviv</span>" — "And brightness was around it" <span class="source">(Yechezkel 1:4)</span>, as brought in the words of our Rebbe, his light shine.<sup>5</sup> (Also, it is brought<sup>6</sup> that <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> corresponds to <span class="key-term">Nogah</span>.) They are also on the four sides — this is an allusion to the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," etc. For when a person falls, G-d forbid, to such places, may the Merciful One save us — then he searches and seeks "Ayeih," etc. And this is his rectification, as above. And this is the aspect of the four sides on which the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are — that one searches and seeks on every side, in all four directions of the world: "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span> — where is the place of His glory, blessed be He?" For the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are in the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>" — through which one is rectified, as above. And this is the allusion of the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> on the four sides: that in every direction one turns, one finds Hashem there — through the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, which are the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>." For the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>" is itself one's rectification, and through this very thing Hashem is found to him, as above.</p>

<!-- =============== Section 3 =============== -->
<h3>§ 3</h3>

<p>And therefore, it is permitted to enter with <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> into a lavatory <span class="source">(Shulchan Aruch, Siman 21, Se'if 3)</span>. And it is brought<sup>7</sup> that this is the aspect of: "<span class="transliteration">Umalchuso bakol mashalah</span>" — "And His kingship rules over all" <span class="source">(Tehillim 103:19)</span>. That is, as above — for the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are in the aspect of the supernal <span class="key-term">Kavod</span>, the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," as above — from which vitality is drawn even to filthy places. And through this very thing, they are subdued, as above.</p>

<p>For through the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> — which are a reminder and sign to remember the Creator, blessed be His Name, and [to remember] that even in those places His kingship, blessed be He, rules — for they have no vitality except from Him, blessed be He — and therefore one searches and seeks on every side: "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span> — the place of His glory," as above. This is in itself the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>" — the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, from which they draw their vitality, as above.</p>

<p>It follows that they return and attach themselves to the very essence of the holiness from which they had been receiving vitality. And this is their subjugation, for their vitality comes only from the concealment of the holiness and its hiddenness with the ultimate concealment. But as soon as one knows that there is holiness there, and one searches and seeks "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," etc., as above — then immediately they return to holiness, and they [the forces of impurity] are subdued.</p>

<p>And this is what is brought in the holy books regarding the law that one is permitted to enter with <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> into a lavatory — that it is the aspect of "His kingship rules over all." For through the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, from which vitality is drawn even to those places — therefore one is permitted to enter with them there, as above. For through this very thing, they are subdued — for "His kingship rules over all," as above.</p>

<p>Therefore, <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> is a <span class="key-term">mitzvah</span> that has no inherent holiness in its body <span class="source">(Megillah 26b)</span> — [its holiness] is concealed and hidden there, as above.</p>

<!-- =============== Section 4 =============== -->
<h3>§ 4</h3>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> of wool and linen, which are the primary <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>. For the primary <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are of wool, which is the aspect of "where is the lamb for the offering?" as above — for the wool of sheep is in a very exalted level, as above. And linen is the opposite, for linen is the aspect of a very low level, as it is written<sup>8</sup> regarding Kayin, who brought from the inferior [produce] — namely, flax [linen].</p>

<p>And because of this very thing, <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are also made from linen. For in flax, which is the lowest level from which the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> draw sustenance — the aspect of Kayin — there specifically is invested a very lofty vitality from the supernal level, namely, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, as above. It follows that linen too receives vitality from the aspect of wool, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, as above. And therefore, <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are made from them as well, for they are in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the prohibition of <span class="key-term">sha'atnez</span> — wool and linen together. For even though in truth, linen too — from which the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> draw sustenance — also receives vitality from the aspect of wool, as above — nevertheless, the primary manner of their reception is through concealment and hiddenness, where the holiness is concealed and hidden there in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, as above. But it is forbidden to reveal the holiness there, so as not to give them too much sustenance, G-d forbid. And therefore, it is forbidden to join wool with linen — for the vitality of the aspect of linen that it receives from the aspect of wool must be in concealment and hiddenness, as above.</p>

<p>But in <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, <span class="key-term">kil'ayim</span> is permitted. For on the contrary — through <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> are subdued, and the holiness is revealed — that even in the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> there had been a very lofty vitality. And therefore, it is permitted there to mix wool and linen together, for in truth both are one — their vitality comes from the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, as above. Only that outside of the context of the <span class="key-term">mitzvah</span> of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, as above — when they are not yet subdued and they still have dominion — one must therefore not join wool with linen, as above, so as not to give them too much vitality. For their vitality must be in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span> — namely, that the aspect of wool, which is the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," should be sealed and concealed and hidden from the aspect of linen, from which the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> draw sustenance. But in the context of the <span class="key-term">mitzvah</span> of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, when the <span class="key-term">chitzonim</span> are subdued, as above — then linen returns together with wool, and they are joined together, for both are truly one aspect, as above.</p>

<!-- =============== Section 5 =============== -->
<h3>§ 5</h3>

<p>And this is the aspect of wrapping oneself in a <span class="key-term">tallis</span> on Yom HaKippurim while it is still day <span class="source">(Shulchan Aruch, Siman 18, Se'if 1, in the Rema)</span>. For the atonement of Yom Kippur is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, which are the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span> — the place of His glory" — which is recited on Yom Kippur in all the <span class="key-term">Kedushos</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the Kedushah prayers]</span>. For Yom Kippur — which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Keser</span> <span class="bracket-def">[Crown — the highest sefirah]</span>, the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>," the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Bereishis</span>" — the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span> that encompasses all the Ten Utterances. For Yom Kippur is the culmination of the Ten Days of <span class="key-term">Teshuvah</span>, which are the aspect of the Ten Utterances.</p>

<p>And this is in itself the aspect of the <span class="key-term">teshuvah</span> and atonement of Yom Kippur — through the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>." For through this aspect, one exits and ascends from all the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>, and all sins are atoned — in the aspect of: "Where [<span class="key-term">ayeih</span>] is the lamb for the offering?" as above. This is revealed on Yom Kippur, when the ashes of Yitzchak are seen before Hashem, as is brought<sup>9</sup> — namely, the aspect of "Where is the lamb for the offering?" as above. And therefore, one wraps oneself in <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> the entire day, for all of this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, which are the aspect of "Where is the lamb for the offering?" as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">tallis shel ratzon</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the tallis of will / favor]</span> in which Hashem wrapped Himself and ordered the Thirteen Attributes of Mercy before Moshe <span class="source">(Rosh Hashanah 17b)</span>. For the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> are the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>" — where there is mercy and favor and atonement, as is brought,<sup>10</sup> and as above.</p>

<!-- =============== Section 6 =============== -->
<h3>§ 6</h3>

<p>And this is the aspect of the fact that the passage of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> was established in <span class="key-term">Krias Shema</span> <span class="source">(see Berachos 12b)</span>, and also that one takes hold of the <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> during <span class="key-term">Krias Shema</span> <span class="source">(Shulchan Aruch, Siman 24, Se'if 2)</span>. For this is the essential matter of <span class="key-term">Krias Shema</span> — to make known and reveal the glory of His kingship, blessed be He. And this is the aspect of: "<span class="transliteration">Shema Yisrael</span>," etc. And with the word "<span class="key-term">Echad</span>" <span class="bracket-def">[One]</span>, we enthrone Him above and below and in the four directions — which is the aspect of: "The entire earth is full of His glory." And we extend the <span class="heb">ד</span> of "<span class="key-term">Echad</span>" — that the <span class="heb">ד</span> should not appear as a <span class="heb">ר</span>, G-d forbid — [for if it were read as <span class="heb">ר</span>, it would spell <span class="heb">אחר</span> — "another"] — in the sense of "My glory I will not give to <em>another</em>."</p>

<p>And behold, since we reveal that Hashem is One and not "another" — from this point on, one wonders: from where do the houses of idol worship and the like receive their vitality? Therefore, we immediately say: "<span class="transliteration">Baruch Sheim K'vod Malchuso l'olam va'ed</span>" — "Blessed is the Name of His glorious kingship forever and ever" — to declare that "His kingship rules over all" — and blessed is the Name of His glory forever and ever, even in the lowest habitation of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>. Only that they receive from the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore we say it quietly. For certainly this is a very great secret, and it is forbidden to contemplate this excessively, all the more so to speak of it — for it is a matter that is extremely concealed and hidden, as brought there in the words of our Rebbe, his light shine. And this is the aspect of: "<span class="zohar-quote">Tzikei k'deirah — tomar yeish lah g'nai, lo tomar</span>," etc. <span class="source">(Pesachim 56a)</span> — that is, one senses lofty holiness in the external places — the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzikei k'deirah</span> <span class="bracket-def">[the fragrant residue of the pot]</span>, which is a fragrant food, but it is found among lowly people. And this is: "'Say: it has disgrace' — 'Do not say: it has pain'" — for one cannot speak of this. Certainly, it is a disgrace to say that there is holiness there. But if one does not say — it has pain, for certainly, in truth, they too receive vitality from the holiness, as above. And therefore they brought it to her quietly — for in secret one reveals that they too receive vitality from Him, blessed be He. Only that it is in the aspect of a secret, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ma'amar sasum</span>, as above.</p>

<p>And this is what is brought<sup>11</sup> — that we say "<span class="key-term">Baruch Sheim K'vod Malchuso l'olam va'ed</span>" quietly, so that they [the forces of impurity] should not overpower us. For in truth, this very thing is their subjugation — that we know that they receive vitality from Him, blessed be He, as above. And therefore, we need to guard ourselves from them, that they should not attack us, since this is their subjugation. (And this is what is brought<sup>12</sup> — that "<span class="key-term">Baruch Sheim K'vod Malchuso l'olam va'ed</span>" corresponds to the aspect of <span class="key-term">Nogah</span>; namely, as above.)</p>

<p>And therefore, on Yom Kippur we say "<span class="key-term">Baruch Sheim K'vod Malchuso l'olam va'ed</span>" aloud. For then the aspect of "<span class="key-term">Ayeih</span>" is revealed, and then is truly their subjugation — for throughout the year he [the Satan] has permission, except on Yom Kippur. And then all sins are atoned and all the <span class="key-term">klipos</span> are nullified. And therefore, then we publicize aloud: "Blessed is the Name of His glorious kingship forever and ever" — namely, that His holiness, blessed be He, is blessed forever even in the habitation of the <span class="key-term">klipos</span>. For they too had been receiving vitality from Him, blessed be He. For now this is not a disgrace at all, since they have now been subdued. For throughout the year, it is somewhat of a disgrace, as it were, to speak of this, as above. But now that they have been subdued, we publicize aloud: "Blessed is the Name of His glorious kingship forever and ever" — namely, that there too the Name of His glory, blessed be He, is blessed, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span> is connected to <span class="key-term">Krias Shema</span> — for all of this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tzitzis</span>, as above.</p>


